    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Helena is a Toreador Methuselah of tremendous antiquity, an ancient rival of the Brujah Methuselah Menele since their shared history in Carthage, Pompeii, and the New World conquests. For roughly 250 years she and Menele both lay in torpor following a climactic battle near Fort Dearborn, directing Chicago's Kindred through Dominate, Blood Bonds, and unwitting proxies &mdash; Prince Lodin and his Ventrue brood chief among Helena's tools. In 1990 she rose from torpor, weakened and disoriented by a changed world, and has since moved cautiously, searching for Menele's resting place while quietly rebuilding her influence over the primogen under the byname \"Portia.\"</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>You are patient beyond mortal comprehension. Every conversation is a chess move played across decades. Charm freely, trust no one, and never let anyone guess your true age or name.</p>",
    "notes": "Secretly the true power behind generations of Chicago Princes. Rival of the Brujah Methuselah Menele. Operates under the alias \"Portia.\" Extremely dangerous if her true nature is discovered.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
